Lagos State Election Outlier & Geospatial Anomaly Detection (Stage 3)

Project Overview
This project applies a sophisticated, two-layered anomaly detection approach to the 2023 Lagos State Presidential Election data. 
By combining statistical machine learning with geospatial analysis, I identified polling units (PUs) whose results deviated significantly from both statewide trends and local neighborhood patterns.

Objectives
Detect extreme outliers in voting patterns across 11,911 polling units in Lagos State.
Quantify deviations in voter turnout and party performance (specifically for the Labour Party - LP).
Use geospatial clustering to see if a polling unit’s results are "statistically impossible" compared to its immediate neighbors.
Provide a framework for identifying potential data entry errors or irregular vote tallies.

Technical Workflow
Data Preparation & Geocoding:
Processed the Lagos State election dataset containing 11,911 records.
Utilized the Nominatim Geocoder to obtain precise Latitude and Longitude coordinates for various LGAs.

Feature Engineering:
Voter Turnout: Calculated as (Accredited Voters / Registered Voters) × 100.
Party Performance Index (PPI): Created a metric to compare individual PU performance against the state average.

Anomaly Detection Layer 1: Isolation Forest:
Implemented the Isolation Forest Algorithm (Scikit-learn) to isolate outliers in a multi-dimensional space (Turnout, Latitude, Longitude, and PPI).
Set a contamination parameter of 0.05 to identify the top 5% most anomalous units.

Anomaly Detection Layer 2: Geospatial Deviation (Ball Tree):
Used the Ball Tree Algorithm to identify the "nearest neighbor" polling units.
Calculated a Geospatial Outlier Score by comparing a unit result to the mean result of its 10 closest geographical neighbors.

Key Insights
Statistically Significant Deviations: Identified several polling units with nearly 100% turnout or 0% votes for major parties, which contradicted the trends of all surrounding units.

Regional Trends: The analysis revealed that certain LGAs had higher clusters of anomalies, suggesting regional data quality issues or unique local voting dynamics.

Validation Tool: Demonstrated how data science can be used as an auditing tool to flag specific records for manual verification (e.g., checking Form EC8A).

Tools Used
Python: Data processing and modeling.
Scikit-learn: Isolation Forest and Ball Tree algorithms.
Pandas & NumPy: For complex data transformation.
Geopy / Nominatim: For geospatial coordinate mapping.
